WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.162
Slope measures output change per unit input change along a nonvertical line

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:12.885
Choose two distinct points, compare their vertical coordinates, and divide by their horizontal separation

00:00:12.885 --> 00:00:18.167
The order of subtraction must stay consistent in numerator and denominator.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:26.132
From negative one, one to three, nine, the horizontal change is four and the vertical change is eight

00:00:26.132 --> 00:00:33.167
Eight divided by four gives slope two: each step right corresponds to a rise of two on this line.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.272
A downward trend gives a negative slope

00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:44.888
Moving from zero, three to two, negative one changes height by negative four across a positive run of two

00:00:44.888 --> 00:00:50.500
The sign records direction, while the magnitude records steepness relative to the axis units.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:58.589
A vertical line has zero horizontal change, so its slope quotient would divide by zero

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:01.305
That slope is undefined, not zero

00:01:01.305 --> 00:01:09.000
Zero slope belongs to a horizontal line, where the height remains unchanged across a nonzero horizontal movement.
